
Application
===========

nio-0.0.1 (alpha)

Description
===========

NIO stands for New IO.

NIO is a new remote display system and also a new internet service.

It consist of a library that can be linked to your programs, a server
(nserver), a client (nlogin), and some example programs.

Basically it is a set of RPC calls to manage a SDL client remotely. It can
be thought of as a poor man's X-Windows, although it is not a desktop
system.

The advantages of nio are:

  - it is internaly simple (so the API can easily be expanded)

  - it is very easy to program for, since the programming model does not
    use events or an object orientation (see example programs).

General Information
===================

Features:

  - Supports usual graphics primitives
  - Has basic terminal support
  - Supports mouse
  - Supports displaying images
  - Supports playing simple tunes and music files

